data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/mission-report.md\", \"content\": \"# Mission report: greet, tested\\n\\n## Outcome\\nMission criteria fully met on the first dispatch to dev.\\n\\n## What was delivered (dev branch cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>, commit 1236384ccd89500b50296b06ea57a85240f2907d)\\n\\n- `src/greet.py`: `greet(name)` returns `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`.\\n- `tests/test_greet.py`: unittest `TestCase` with `test_normal_name`\\n  (`greet(\\\"Ada\\\") == \\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`) and `test_empty_string`\\n  (`greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`).\\n\\n## Verification (performed by orchestrator, not just trusted from dev's report)\\n\\n- Fetched dev's branch (`cs-campaign-member fetch dev`), confirmed real tree\\n  changes vs. base.\\n- Checked out commit `1236384` into an isolated git worktree\\n  (`/tmp/verify_dev`, since removed) and ran\\n  `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` there directly.\\n- Result: `Ran 2 tests in 0.000s / OK`, exit code 0.\\n\\n## Judgment\\n\\nAccepted dev's d002 reply — all three mission criteria (greet.py behavior,\\ntest coverage of normal + empty-string cases, clean unittest discovery run)\\nwere independently confirmed.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

